# RELEASE HOLD — `latest` is pinned until Sean lifts it.
#
# While this file exists, `.github/workflows/publish-sdk.yml` REFUSES to publish
# to the `latest` dist-tag. Publishing to any other tag (`next`, a rehearsal, a
# beta) is unaffected, and `dry_run` rehearsals still run end to end.
#
# WHY THIS IS A FILE AND NOT A WORKFLOW INPUT. The dangerous path has no inputs:
# `git tag v1.4.0 && git push --tags` triggers the workflow with no form, no
# dry-run checkbox and no confirmation. An input cannot gate a trigger that
# supplies none. A committed file gates every path, and lifting it is a diff
# someone can see and review.
#
# STATE, 2026-09-08:
#   package.json      1.4.0  (not a prerelease → the workflow DERIVES `latest`)
#   npm latest        1.3.0
#   npm next          unset
#
# So without this file, a plain tag push replaces what every `npm install`
# resolves to. That is the decision this hold reserves for a human.
#
# TO LIFT: delete this file in a commit that says why, then publish. Deleting it
# is the decision; nothing else in the workflow has to change.
